zoonosis|Noun|an animal disease that can be transmitted to humans
zoonotic|Adjective|of or relating to or constituting zoonosis - "the Ebola virus is believed to be zoonotic"
zoophilia|Noun|a sexual attraction to animals
zoophobia|Noun|a morbid fear of animals
zoophyte|Noun|any of various invertebrate animals resembling a plant such as a sea anemone or coral or sponge
zooplankton|Noun|animal constituent of plankton;mainly small crustaceans and fish larvae
zoopsia|Noun|visual hallucination of animals;sometimes occurring in delirium tremens
zoospore|Noun|an asexual spore of some algae and fungi that moves by means of flagella
Zoroaster|Noun|Persian prophet who founded Zoroastrianism (circa 628-551 BC)
