zymase|Noun|a complex of enzymes that cause glycolysis;originally found in yeast but also present in higher organisms
zymoid|Adjective|resembling an enzyme
zymology|Noun|the branch of chemistry concerned with fermentation (as in making wine or brewing or distilling)
